  "details": "libssh is a library which implements the SSH protocol. It can be used to implement client and server applications.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * libssh: libssh: denial of service via zero advertised channel packet size (CVE-2026-59843)\n  * libssh: libssh: denial of service via oversized SFTP read length (CVE-2026-59844)\n  * libssh: libssh: denial of service via unchecked ProxyCommand fork() failure (CVE-2026-59845)\n  * libssh: libssh: information disclosure via ProxyCommand %r username expansion (CVE-2026-59846)\n  * libssh: libssh: integrity downgrade via OpenSSL AES-GCM tag verification (CVE-2026-59847)\n  * libssh: libssh: denial of service via SFTP responses with unknown request IDs (CVE-2026-59848)\n  * libssh: libssh: use-after-free via data callbacks on closed channels (CVE-2026-59850)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
